{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nYou write of my illness with such alarm, and Immanuel asks what caused it? It was merely the damp cold and a bad digestion, nothing more. I am well now.\n\nI spent the morning with Cousin. He is a clever man, though he talks too much about \"spirit\" without having read the *Phenomenology*. He insisted on paying for my dinner at the Café de Paris—four francs for a mediocre soup and a glass of claret. I let him, as it is a fine way to settle accounts. The wine was ordinary, but the company was livelier than usual.\n\nI walked the Tuileries in the late afternoon. The light on the Seine was quite beautiful, but the crowds are thick with tourists. I bought a small snuff box for two francs to replace the one I lost in Berlin.\n\nI am not ill, only tired. Tell Karl to stop worrying so much, or he will be the next one to fall.\n\nYour loving husband,\nG.W.F."}}],"created":1795219275,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":218,"prompt_tokens":1088,"total_tokens":1306,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-am6slVcvkn20GFdZANra56YFWUSQoWR6","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":1088,"prompt_ms":1111.811,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.0218851102941175,"prompt_per_second":978.5835901965353,"predicted_n":218,"predicted_ms":5106.905,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.53412442396313,"predicted_per_second":42.491489463775025}}